prereg itself named, p=1.0, no significance reachable regardless of true
effect size. Secondary fidelity: 4W/2L/5T, p=0.6875. Mechanism-level
secondary (does engine-visibility help refinement at all): 9W/0L/2T,
p=0.00390625 -- replicates the identical signal from the prior incomplete
24-cell run.

Reading, per the prereg's own pre-committed terms: the fix worked (a real,
complete measurement now exists where before there was only a blocked one);
it does NOT overturn the 2026-08-03 closure of the single-shot-GGUF-induction
axis -- it confirms the closure was correct, now definitively rather than by
default. Recorded in ops/known-issues.md as a progress-log addendum (never
replacing the original directive). Per the Failed-Experiment Rerun
Discipline, the axis stays closed -- no further rerun on this corpus chasing
more discordant primary games.

